g that  they can by now  what else can they do what more have  they got to give that is exactly point  that in fact they should be able to be a  little bit more vigorous and taking some  of the risks because these things are  not or not easy issues they should take  some risks to be able to salvage the  nuclear deal otherwise it cannot be  continued the way it is and if they  don't your government's prepared to go  back to enriching uranium we are for the  moment engaged in enriching uranium but  there are certain parameters and we are  bound to in fact to implement our  commitments including the enrichment  uranium within those parameters but we  have said that if these cannot be  sustained  we were suspending some of those  parameters and we would be beyond some  of those parameters defined in the  nuclear deal and people like Jeremy Hunt  the British Foreign Secretary he said  there will be grave consequences for  Iran if you do so does that not worry  you there would be certainly grave  consequences from Iran if they would not  be able to find a solution and we have  we have already elaborated that what are  those consequences and if in certain day  60 days would not be a solution Iran  would be implementing its second phase  measures that has has been announced and  certainly the situation would be worse  and we hope that in fact they would take  this message from Iran very seriously  and find a solution but is your  government in a position to be setting  out ultimatums to Europeans who say  they're doing what they can to try and  make this deal work it's not ultimatum  it's only call for effective  implementation of the deal there is a  deal that has been multilateral  achievement  and the success of the multilateral  diplomacy and what Iran is is is asking  is the implementation of the deal  looking at what America is doing they've  moved b-52 bombers to the region they've  moved an aircraft carrier Strike Group  they're talking about 120,000 soldiers  possi